<p>My reaction is mostly personal. The story just didn't interest me enough to justify the lengthy slog. One thing that I'm going to nitpick, however:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Mark P█████</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What is the point of this? Why would you only censor this much? Why is it acceptable to know the first letter of the person's last name but not the rest? From an in-universe standpoint, using the information that is left unredacted, anyone could determine the real identities of the persons involved with a ten minute Google search. If it's important to have the names in the story, then I would just leave the names in. If it's unimportant, just blackbox the whole thing. I've never understood blackboxing things in this manner.</p>

